the make or break of the native-total story measured: ALBW 600 frames
AOT, three runs on Apple M1 Pro — software renderer 471.2 MIPS,
hardware rasterizer with CPU vertex shading 2409.1 MIPS (1.12s),
hardware with GPU shading 357.0 MIPS (7.53s, gpu 6.3s): the fork's
default of CPU shading on integrated devices stands measured.

rasterize counts the two buckets (the re-walk hands its count over);
the app totals frames, the slowest half-second window and the underruns
all told, and logs one session kpi line as it exits; headless prints
the buckets as it reports.
